  => STEP 8 PASS: the IPv4 restriction survives a reboot, and it survives it on the wire.
     The DUT saved it as `service ssh ipv6`.  After a 60 second cold boot, with nothing typed
     into the device, IPv4 TCP port 22 refused 4 of 4 SYNs while ICMP answered 4 of 4 to the
     same address.  The port 23 control answered RA in all four legs, so the instrument was
     reading RA correctly throughout.  The full arc on the wire is SA -> RA -> (cold boot)
     RA -> SA.  The restriction was then removed.  `service ssh` is back to its plain form
